The report range is not exactly the current calendar month or year; no current-period projection is computed.
Basis:
No sample window is stated; as of 4 Jan 2026.
Updates:
This forecast updates as data arrives. Projected figures never enter an actual table or total.
Report notes
•
Some purchase orders in this range carry a retired whole-order discount or adjustment. The amount includes it, but it is not supplier cost and
no margin is inferred from it.
Definitions
•
PPN is excluded from every amount, costed amount, capital and margin figure in this report. The customer pays PPN on top of a quotation; it
is collected for the state and is never profit.
•
Capital is the pinned source revision's pre-margin unit cost at the purchase order's quantity, rounded once per purchase order. It is not the
quotation's sell price and it is not the latest revision's cost.
•
PO margin is costed amount minus capital. It covers only purchase orders whose source cost resolved; uncosted amount is never counted as
profit. PPH23 is not subtracted: this is a PO margin, not the quotation's nett profit.
•
Corrections are counted once at their current values. A correction can move a purchase order between periods, so this report reflects current
records, not the values as they stood when each order was received.
•
Current-period projections are estimates from elapsed days or complete months. They are drawn as hatched ghosts with a low-high range,
never styled as actuals, and never included in an actual table or total.
•
Partial and in-progress periods are marked in the period table. They should not be compared with complete periods as if the same amount of
time had passed.
•
All money is in IDR and no figure is converted between currencies. Counts may combine currencies only within the selected one; money
never does.
